      ":question/problem": "The cost, $C(x)$, and revenue, $R(x)$, functions, in dollars, of a private school are given by\n$C(x) = 600 + 6.6x, R(x) = 10x - 0.002x^{2}$,\nwhere $x$ represents the number of students enrolled in the school. Find the value of $x$ for which the school breaks even.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
